WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Glacier Time Machine: Muir Inlet, Alaska on the real Copernicus elevation model

2
00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:14.006
Fly up the inlet on the real elevation model — no vertical exaggeration

3
00:00:14.006 --> 00:00:15.508
Skip any cinematic from the first frame (Esc)

4
00:00:15.508 --> 00:00:22.517
Same place, different time: the USGS repeat photographs, 1941 to 2004

5
00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:30.518
The glacier retreated more than 3 km in nine years — and more than 7 km by 2004

6
00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:35.522
Measure the retreat yourself along the valley path

7
00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:39.526
Rates are computed only from the published anchor points, and labelled as lower bounds

8
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:44.529
What came next: succession after the ice, with the evidence sorted for you to judge

9
00:00:44.529 --> 00:00:49.532
Every claim shows its source; the surface colours are labelled an approximation

10
00:00:49.532 --> 00:00:54.038
Every task also works in text mode, with the same data

11
00:00:54.038 --> 00:00:58.042
Free, no account, no tracking: immersive-learning-showcase.vercel.app
